v1.3.6 (2026-05-12)
-------------------
Installer reliability fixes — tested on fresh Windows PC.

Installer (setup.nsi / VPNSetup.exe):
- Fixed: pip install now works on truly fresh PCs — removed --no-index so PyPI
  is used as fallback for any wheel not in the bundle
- Fixed: added missing Windows-only wheels: pywin32, pywin32-ctypes, colorama
  (Linux pip does not resolve Windows-conditional deps; these were absent from
  the bundle and caused pip exit 1 on fresh machines)
- Fixed: OpenVPN Connect now installs silently — changed winget override from
  /S (NSIS flag, wrong) to /qn (MSI completely-silent flag); suppresses EULA
  dialog during install
- Fixed: OpenVPN Connect install is now synchronous (nsExec blocking) so the
  "Installation complete" message only appears after it finishes
- Fixed: installer log now written by Python subprocess (not cmd /c) so it
  works on corporate PCs where cmd.exe may be restricted
- Added: C:\Users\Public\vpnlog.txt — full pip output log for diagnostics;
  easy to find compared to %LOCALAPPDATA%

Debugging:
- vpnlog.txt at C:\Users\Public\vpnlog.txt captures Python path, version,
  and full pip output — share with admin if installation fails
